+# Task: Compare, classify, report (P25-09) Phase: 25 Owner: wave-41 builder Q1
+
+Read (reference @ `ab3fe9dffb0a89d534cb795e2a2940e5f6542056`): none — skill reference 03 §6–§7
+and §10 (comparison halves, classification, limits). REA's `compare_web_captures` contract as its
+MCP server published it (third-party tool). No reference capture exists in this sandbox and the
+reference app was never run here.
+Evidence: none of the reference.
+
+What it does (own words): puts a flow's product capture next to the reference capture of the
+same flow and lists what differs, aligned by exact step id. Kinds: `step-only-in-<side>`,
+`step-failed-in-<side>`, `role-only-in-<side>` (structural kinds seen at a `wait_for` step on one
+side only — accessibility roles for browser flows, card kinds and prompts for terminal flows,
+message key paths for stdio and platform flows; names and text never compared; non-`wait_for`
+steps never compared, because each app races its own update after an action) and `page-errors`.
+Duplicate step ids or different origins are alignment failures: that flow is not compared and
+counts as unclassified. Each divergence is classified with `rules.json`: a reference gap (its
+step is listed as one the reference cannot do), intended (a rule matches scenario, kind and
+subject and cites a D-id), else unclassified. `compare_all` writes `<flow>.compare.json` (summary,
+counts) and `<flow>.divergences.json`; the runner exits 1 while anything is unclassified.
+REA's own step-aligned comparison runs through its MCP tools on the same captures (the runner has
+no MCP client); its result goes next to ours in `~/rea-lab/parity/indus/`.
+
+Inputs → outputs: `python scripts/parity/compare.py PRODUCT REFERENCE [--rules FILE]` → JSON
+result, exit 1 while unclassified; `runner.py --all --ref DIR [--out DIR]` → per-flow files and
+the count; `docs/internals/parity-report-v1.md` → commands, versions, counts, limits.
+
+Files: `scripts/parity/compare.py`, `tests/unit/parity/test_compare.py`,
+`tests/fixtures/parity/captures/*.json` (synthetic, generated by us), `docs/internals/parity-report-v1.md`.
+
+Edge cases / failure modes: REA results load wrapped (`normalized_result`) or bare; the
+`scenario_start` step is skipped; an accessibility snapshot's quoted lines (`- 'button "…"'`) and
+link URL lines are handled; a step only one side has and that failed there gives both kinds.
+
+Our design differences / decisions: none user-visible. 16-what-we-change.md is unchanged: no
+capture contradicts it yet (there is no reference capture).
+
+Tests we will write: synthetic pair → the exact divergence list; roles only at `wait_for`; names
+ignored; duplicate ids and different origins fail alignment; classification intended / gap /
+unclassified with counts; `compare_all` writes both files and returns the unclassified count;
+terminal captures compare cards and prompts; the CLI exits 1 while unclassified.
+
+## Decisions for the lead
+- The final run the row asks for ("0 unclassified, ledger 0 open, 0 failed") needs the reference
+  captures from the owner's REA sandbox: owed. Product side: 0 failed.
+- Product observation to triage (not a parity divergence): in the TUI model picker a custom
+  endpoint shows "this provider lists no models: type a model id", while the same endpoint's
+  `GET /v1/models` lists six models and `indus setup` offers them. Typing an id works.
+
+Compare checklist (filled after the rewrite; reopened skill reference 03 §6, §7, §10):
+- [x] kinds `step-only-in-<side>`, `step-failed-in-<side>`, `role-only-in-<side>` at `wait_for` only, `page-errors` (`tests/unit/parity/test_compare.py::test_divergences_of_the_synthetic_pair`, `::test_roles_are_compared_only_at_wait_for_steps`)
+- [x] names not compared (`::test_accessible_names_are_ignored`)
+- [x] duplicate ids / origins are alignment failures (`::test_duplicate_ids_are_an_alignment_failure`, `::test_different_origins_are_an_alignment_failure`)
+- [x] every divergence classified or counted; exit 1 while unclassified (`::test_classification_intended_gap_unclassified`, `::test_main_exits_1_while_unclassified`)
+- [x] report with commands, versions, counts, limits (`docs/internals/parity-report-v1.md`)
+- Not taken: screenshot side-by-side review (needs the reference captures).
+
+## Status
+
+Partial (2026-10-21): tooling, tests and the report are done; the comparison itself waits for the
+owner's reference captures.
